# Copy this file to `.env` in the project directory, then fill in at least one key.
#
#   Linux/macOS   cp .env.example .env
#   Windows       copy .env.example .env        (PowerShell: Copy-Item .env.example .env)
#
# `.env` is gitignored — this file holds a credential that spends your money, so it
# never gets committed and never gets pasted into a terminal screenshot.
#
# A key is needed only for `score-job`, `rank`, `tailor` and `record-fixtures`. `collect`,
# `jobs`, `ats`, `closing` and `start-here` run without one.
#
# EVERY key below is a free tier that needs no credit card. The tool tries `config.py`
# MODEL_CHAIN in order and silently skips the hops you did not fill in, so one key works
# and every extra key is another day-sized window. Run `careerpilot keys` to see which
# hops are live on your machine and which one is worth getting next.
#
# Groq and Gemini meter tokens per MODEL per day, so the chain gives each of them two
# models: when gpt-oss-120b spends its 200,000 tokens, gpt-oss-20b on the same key is a
# separate window that is still open.

# Hops 1 and 3 — console.groq.com. Fastest, and the default.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Hops 2 and 4 — Google AI Studio (aistudio.google.com). The single most useful second
# key: it is the difference between "come back tomorrow" and working now.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Hops 5 and 6 — openrouter.ai. One key, many `:free` models behind an OpenAI-compatible
# endpoint. Metered per request per day, so it answers even when both token budgets are
# spent. Both ids declare structured_outputs in OpenRouter's own public list.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Hop 7 — cerebras.ai. A third free token budget, same wire format as Groq. Model id taken
# from their public list, never exercised from a key on this machine.
CEREBRAS_API_KEY=

# Hop 8 — cohere.com. Last, because Chat V2 has no response_format: the JSON is asked for
# in the prompt and validated afterwards, so a refusal to comply costs a hop rather than
# shipping a bad bullet. Also unexercised here — no key on this machine.
COHERE_API_KEY=

# Real model calls are opt-in and off by default, so that tests and CI can never
# spend money by accident. Without this line the tool replays recorded answers and
# refuses to invent one for a prompt it has never seen.
CAREERPILOT_LIVE=1
